kcp-go — internal/thirdparty/kcp-go (a modified copy)
https://github.com/xtaci/kcp-go v5.6.72, MIT licence

KCP is the PCK engine's reliable stream, and it too is built from a copy kept in
this repository (go.mod replaces the module with it). Four things were added,
and each is off until a session asks for it, so the other users of kcp-go in
Backpack run as before: a retransmission margin the window control sets, so
that the timer does not fire for segments a queue it allows is still holding; a
fast retransmission that can itself be fast-retransmitted, instead of waiting
for the timer; a reading of the delay that received data met (from the
timestamp every data segment already carries), which lets the window control
tell its own direction's queue from the other's; and a larger output queue, for
the rate limiter. The wire format is unchanged. The changes are marked
"Backpack" in kcp.go and sess.go. The upstream licence is in
internal/thirdparty/kcp-go/LICENSE and applies to the copy:

